## Control {{controlId}}: Provide Controls on Tools, Techniques, Mechanisms, and Personnel Used for System Maintenance

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization controls maintenance tools, techniques, and personnel within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through approved tool inventories and personnel authorization documented in "Maintenance Controls Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

**Approved Maintenance Tools:**
- **Administration Portals:** Azure Government portal, Microsoft 365 admin center, Exchange admin center, Intune admin console — all accessed via authenticated, encrypted sessions
- **PowerShell Modules:** Microsoft Graph PowerShell SDK, Exchange Online Management, Teams PowerShell — approved versions maintained in tool inventory
- **Remote Access:** Azure AD-joined management workstations with MFA and Conditional Access enforcement
- **Diagnostics:** Microsoft Support and Recovery Assistant (SaRA), Microsoft 365 Network Connectivity Test

**Personnel Authorization:**
- Only personnel with designated administrative roles may perform maintenance
- Maintenance personnel verified through background check and security clearance process
- Vendor maintenance (Microsoft support) conducted under supervision with time-limited access

{{#if pimConfigured}}
**Privileged Maintenance Access:**
PIM enforces just-in-time elevation for maintenance roles, ensuring maintenance access is time-bound and audited.
{{/if}}

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Maintain approved tool inventory; annual review of maintenance tool authorization; vendor access requires written authorization
- **Frequency:** Annual tool review, per-incident vendor authorization
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Documentation:** Maintenance Controls Policy v1.0, Approved Tool Inventory

**Review Frequency:** Annually by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine approved tool inventory, maintenance personnel authorization records, PIM activation logs for maintenance roles, and vendor access logs.

